WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.320
These days, a hit movie getting a sequel&nbsp;
isn't much of a surprise — in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:09.280
it's usually a given. Nonetheless, there are&nbsp;
a few projects in the work that nobody could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.640
possibly have seen coming. Here are the sequels&nbsp;
you probably had no idea were even happening.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:21.120
It's been almost 20 years since audiences first&nbsp;
followed sorority girl Elle Woods to Harvard Law&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.000
School in the bubblegum comedy Legally Blonde.&nbsp;
The movie was followed up with 2003's Legally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.680
Blonde 2: Red, White &amp; Blonde, and now Elle&nbsp;
is back in an as-yet-untitled threequel. ,

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.200
Not much has been said in the way of plot&nbsp;
details, although sources originally told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.840
Deadline that the third movie will be "much in&nbsp;
the spirit of the first film," which saw Elle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:45.680
draw on her fashion sense, optimism, and strong&nbsp;
sense of sisterhood to defy the patriarchy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.520
lift up the women around&nbsp;
her… and look great doing it.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.360
"You got into Harvard Law?"

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.440
"What, like it's hard?"

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.840
That Deadline report mostly referred&nbsp;
to an earlier draft of the script,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.560
before Office alum Mindy Kaling and Brooklyn&nbsp;
Nine-Nine creator Dan Goor took over writing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.960
duties — but it's easy to imagine that the&nbsp;
new story will also embrace the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.640
movie's themes of female empowerment. Legally&nbsp;
Blonde 3 is expected to arrive in May 2022.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.320
When The Meg first swam into theaters,&nbsp;
plenty of people were skeptical at what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:24.000
appeared to be an over-the-top Jaws ripoff.&nbsp;
But this megalodon movie earned some serious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:31.760
coin at the box office, drawing $528 million&nbsp;
worldwide against its $130 million budget. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.360
maybe that's not really so surprising —&nbsp;
after all, it's basically a movie about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.400
Jason Statham going to war with a gigantic&nbsp;
shark. Who doesn't want to see that?

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.200
Well, after audiences went into a feeding frenzy&nbsp;
for the film, plans for a sequel were almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:50.160
immediately set into motion. In October 2020,&nbsp;
Warner Bros. confirmed that, of all people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.520
the critically-acclaimed thriller filmmaker Ben&nbsp;
Wheatley will be helming the shark-tastic sequel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.920
Nobody's really sure what the plot will&nbsp;
be, but since The Meg is actually based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:05.520
on a series of books by Steve Alten, the sequel&nbsp;
might well draw on the next novel, which involves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:12.069
an even bigger shark, as well as the giant,&nbsp;
crocodile-like beast known as the Kronosaurus .

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:19.040
In 2007, Disney captivated audiences with&nbsp;
Enchanted, a princess story with a twist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.680
in which the animated princess Giselle&nbsp;
accidentally tumbles into real-world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.480
live-action New York City. Although Giselle&nbsp;
eventually found her happy ending with single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.200
dad Robert, that didn't stop talk of a sequel&nbsp;
from spinning soon after the film's release.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.720
While the sequel, titled Disenchanted,&nbsp;
was slow getting off the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.920
the production is now full steam ahead, and&nbsp;
will be premiering exclusively on Disney+ .

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.480
In 2016, Hairspray director Adam Shankman&nbsp;
was brought on board to direct the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.760
and he confirmed in 2019 that he's&nbsp;
still attached to the production.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.680
The script for Disenchanted is said to&nbsp;
take place ten years after the first film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.400
following Giselle as she questions her&nbsp;
happily ever after — and inadvertently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:03.200
shakes things up in both the real world&nbsp;
and the animated kingdom of Andalasia .

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.440
Disney has confirmed that Amy Adams will&nbsp;
return for the sequel, and while Patrick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.080
Dempsey hasn't been officially announced as a&nbsp;
cast member, he has told Entertainment Tonight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:17.840
that he'd happily be involved, just so long as the&nbsp;
sequel can live up to the magic of the original.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.760
Nearly a quarter century after the&nbsp;
release of the first Scream movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.800
a fifth installment in the deliciously self-aware&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.200
horror franchise has wrapped filming&nbsp;
— and is headed to theaters in 2022.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.760
Stars Courteney Cox and David Arquette have&nbsp;
appeared in all four previous Scream installments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.400
and both officially signed on for the fifth&nbsp;
film in 2020. Although Cox and Arquette are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.720
divorced in real life, their characters should&nbsp;
theoretically still be married in the films.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.920
Marley Shelton, who played Judy Hicks in Scream&nbsp;
4, will also be returning, as will NeveCampbell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.000
who played protagonist Sidney Prescott&nbsp;
in all four prior Scream films. Although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.440
Campbell's casting was never officially&nbsp;
announced by Campell or the studio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:59.280
her involvement was confirmed when Kevin&nbsp;
Williamson tweeted a photo of himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.560
alongside Campbell and Cox announcing the end&nbsp;
of filming. In a caption, Williamson wrote:

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.640
"I'm thrilled to be reunited with&nbsp;
Neve, Courteney, David and Marley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:13.920
and to be working alongside a new filmmaking&nbsp;
team and incredible cast of newcomers that have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:19.040
come together to continue Wes's legacy with the&nbsp;
upcoming relaunch of the franchise that I hold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.800
so dear to my heart. See you&nbsp;
in theatres January 2022."

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:29.680
In 2015, Mad Max: Fury Road reinvigorated&nbsp;
the long-dormant Mad Max franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:34.560
offering a thrilling new spin on George&nbsp;
Miller's post-apocalyptic action series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:39.360
Casting Tom Hardy as Max and shifting the&nbsp;
focus to Charlize Theron's rage-fueled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:46.160
Imperator Furiosa , Fury Road wowed audiences&nbsp;
and critics alike, with many now considering it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:52.560
one of the best action films of all time. So it&nbsp;
seemed that a sequel was pretty much inevitable.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.360
And sure enough, five years after Fury Road&nbsp;
roared into theaters, two follow-up films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:02.000
are in the works. One is a direct sequel&nbsp;
to Fury Road, while the other is a prequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:07.200
centered around a younger Furiosa. The sequel,&nbsp;
which has been given the working title Mad Max:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.760
The Wasteland, was reportedly greenlit by&nbsp;
Warner Bros. in early 2020, and while the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:16.960
movie will follow the further exploits of&nbsp;
Max, Furiosa herself isn't set to return.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.680
Of course, Furiosa will bring back the character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.120
but Theron won't be making an&nbsp;
appearance in that film either;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:28.000
director George Miller said that much as he loved&nbsp;
Theron's performance in Fury Road, he doesn't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.320
enough faith in de-aging technology to allow&nbsp;
Theron to reprise her role for the prequel.

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:35.520
Instead, the younger Furiosa will&nbsp;
be played by Anya Taylor-Joy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:41.840
who will be joined by MCU star Chris Hemsworth and&nbsp;
Emmy-winning Watchmen actor Yahya Abdul-Mateen II&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:45.920
in undisclosed roles. However, their&nbsp;
characters have likely existed in Miller's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:50.960
head since before the previous film, since he&nbsp;
developed origin stories for every character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:56.000
while prepping Fury Road — even writing an&nbsp;
entire screenplay for Furiosa in the process.

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:02.400
In an act of divine providence — or maybe&nbsp;
just Hollywood nostalgia — it looks like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.240
Sister Mary Clarence will be donning&nbsp;
her habit once again. In late 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:10.160
Whoopi Goldberg announced that&nbsp;
Sister Act 3 is finally in the works,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.440
after years of being told that there&nbsp;
was no interest in a threequel.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.880
The film, which will premiere on&nbsp;
Disney+, was confirmed by Disney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.440
at their 2020 Investor Day event. Goldberg&nbsp;
will be returning as both star and producer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.920
with Tyler Perry also coming on board to&nbsp;
produce. Released in 1992, the first Sister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:31.200
Act saw Goldberg play Deloris Van Cartier , a&nbsp;
lounge singer who goes into witness protection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:36.160
at a convent after witnessing a killing. There,&nbsp;
in the guise of a nun named Sister Mary Clarence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:42.000
Deloris transforms the convent's humdrum&nbsp;
choir into an upbeat musical sensation.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:47.120
Sister Act got a sequel in 1993 with Sister&nbsp;
Act 2: Back in the Habit, which found Deloris&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:51.360
stepping in as a music teacher for a group of&nbsp;
low-achieving students at a Catholic school.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:56.480
And while Goldberg hasn't dropped any hints about&nbsp;
the plot of Sister Act 3, it's safe to assume that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:01.600
Deloris will likely be giving a lackluster&nbsp;
singing group a powerful musical makeover.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:05.120
It hasn't yet been confirmed whether the&nbsp;
recurring cast members from the previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:09.600
movies will be returning, but Goldberg herself&nbsp;
seems keen to bring them back into the fold.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:17.200
"So we're working diligently to try to figure out&nbsp;
how to get every — how to get the gang together."

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:22.560
While Hocus Pocus failed to make much of a splash&nbsp;
when it was first released in 1993, it has since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:27.680
gathered a cult following as a Halloween staple.&nbsp;
The film follows a group of kids who accidentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:33.280
resurrect a trio of sisters on Halloween, three&nbsp;
hundred years after their execution in 1693.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:37.600
While details on the sequel remain scarce,&nbsp;
original Hocus Pocus writer Mick Garris has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:42.080
suggested that, although himself is not involved,&nbsp;
he's under the impression that original stars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:47.360
Bette Midler, Kathy Najimy , and Sarah Jessica&nbsp;
Parker are set to return. Those three have indeed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:51.440
all expressed an interest in the movie, so&nbsp;
now that Hocus Pocus 2 has been officially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:55.760
confirmed by Disney, it would be surprising if&nbsp;
they didn't make at least a brief appearance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:00.720
Hocus Pocus 2 is expected to debut on Disney+&nbsp;
sometime in the not-too-distant future.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:06.960
Released in 2010, David Fincher and Aaron Sorkin's&nbsp;
The Social Network earned tremendous critical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:12.800
acclaim and won three Oscars for its screenplay,&nbsp;
editing, and score. Now, a decade later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:17.520
Sorkin is eager to return to the story of Mark&nbsp;
Zuckerberg's tech empire, this time looking into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:23.280
what Facebook has become and the role it plays&nbsp;
in modern politics. Speaking to MTV's "Happy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:27.840
Sad Confused" podcast about the possibility&nbsp;
of a Social Network sequel, Sorkin said:

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:32.160
"I do want to see it. And [producer Scott&nbsp;
Rudin wants to see it. People have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:36.560
talking to me about it because of what we've&nbsp;
discovered is the dark side of Facebook."

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:38.640
Although Sorkin and Rudin seem to be on board,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:43.200
there's one thing that could still stand in the&nbsp;
way of The Social Network 2 becoming a reality:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:46.720
a commitment from director David&nbsp;
Fincher. Working explained:

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.040
"I will only write it if David directs&nbsp;
it. If Billy Wilder came back from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:54.640
grave and said he wanted to direct it,&nbsp;
I'd say I'd only do it with David."

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.880
In addition to Jesse Eisenberg , The Social&nbsp;
Network starred a number of other talented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.080
young actors — and although it's safe&nbsp;
to assume that The Social Network 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:05.120
would see Eisenberg return to his&nbsp;
role, there's no knowing which of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:08.800
his fellow Social Network cast members&nbsp;
might make an appearance in the sequel.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:13.360
After the massive commercial success&nbsp;
of Disney's Lion King remake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.720
it seemed like only a matter of time&nbsp;
until a sequel was announced. But the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:20.080
follow-up's director is more of&nbsp;
a surprise — because this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:24.880
Academy Award-winning writer and director Barry&nbsp;
Jenkins will be sitting in the director's chair.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:29.680
Jenkins won't be writing The Lion King 2, but&nbsp;
will be working from a script by Jeff Nathanson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:33.920
who penned the first movie. While no specific&nbsp;
details of the plot have been revealed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:37.920
Deadline reports that "the story will further&nbsp;
explore the mythology of the characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:42.960
including Mufasa's origin story." Although The&nbsp;
Lion King 2 seems like an outlier in Jenkins'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:47.760
filmography, which includes movies such as&nbsp;
Moonlight and If Beale Street Could Talk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:52.160
the director seems excited about working on&nbsp;
the sequel. In a statement, Jenkins said:

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:56.800
"Having the opportunity to work with Disney on&nbsp;
expanding this magnificent tale of friendship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:59.920
love and legacy, while furthering&nbsp;
my work chronicling the lives and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:03.840
souls of folk within the African&nbsp;
diaspora, is a dream come true."

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:10.160
During Disney's 2020 Investor Day event, the&nbsp;
studio reaffirmed that a fifth installment in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:16.000
the iconic Indiana Jones franchise is on the&nbsp;
way, and will once again star Indy himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:22.960
Harrison Ford. At 78 years old, Ford will likely&nbsp;
be retiring his trademark whip and fedora by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:27.440
end of Indiana Jones 5, although the studio&nbsp;
hasn't yet indicated whether the film will see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:31.840
him pass the baton to a younger generation&nbsp;
— or close out the franchise altogether.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:35.680
"It's not the years, honey. It's the mileage."

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.600
James Mangold is sitting in the&nbsp;
director's chair for the new movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:44.800
and if anybody knows how to bring the legacy&nbsp;
of a beloved action hero to a dignified end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:49.920
it's him. Mangold previously directed 2017's&nbsp;
Logan, which earned him an Academy Award&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:55.760
nomination for Best Adapted Screenplay, and served&nbsp;
as a thrilling and satisfying conclusion for Hugh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.760 --> 00:11:00.560
Jackman and Patrick Stewart's characters.&nbsp;
While Indiana Jones 5 isn't likely to skew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:05.920
nearly as dark as Logan, fans can only hope&nbsp;
that it will provide a similarly moving farewell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:10.880
to everybody's favorite adventurer.&nbsp;
Indy 5 hits theaters in July 2022.

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:16.880
In October 2020, actor Stephen Lang revealed on&nbsp;
Twitter that he'd just wrapped filming on Don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:22.240
Breathe 2, the sequel to the 2016 home invasion&nbsp;
horror thriller. In the first film, Lang played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:27.680
the cryptically named Blind Man, a homeowner who&nbsp;
finds himself the target of a trio of small-scale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:32.800
burglars. Unfortunately for the would-be thieves,&nbsp;
the Blind Man is far more capable and ruthless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:37.040
than they assume, and winds up trapping&nbsp;
them in a deadly game of cat and mouse.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:40.640
The sequel follows Lang's character&nbsp;
several years after the home invasion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:45.600
as the Blind Man lives in quiet isolation with&nbsp;
a young girl who was orphaned by a house fire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:49.520
The Blind Man is forced to jump back into&nbsp;
action when the girl is kidnapped, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:54.640
and if the first movie is any indication, the&nbsp;
kidnappers have no idea what they're in for.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:12:01.120
After six successful movies very loosely based&nbsp;
on the video game series of the same name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:06.720
Resident Evil is finally getting a proper origin&nbsp;
story, jumping back to the events of the earliest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:11.840
games in the series. This standalone Resident&nbsp;
Evil prequel will star Kaya Scodelario as Claire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:17.120
Redfield, Hannah John-Kamen as Jill Valentine,&nbsp;
Robbie Amell as Chris Redfield, Tom Hopper as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:22.880
Albert Wesker, Avan Jogia as Leon Kennedy,&nbsp;
and Neal McDonough as William Birkin . The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:27.680
film will be written and directed by Johannes&nbsp;
Roberts, who said of his approach to the film:

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:31.360
"With this movie, I really wanted to&nbsp;
go back to the original first two games&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:35.920
and re-create the terrifying visceral&nbsp;
experience I had when I first played them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:40.240
whilst at the same time telling a grounded&nbsp;
human story about a small dying American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:44.160
town that feels both relatable and&nbsp;
relevant to today's audiences."

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:48.480
Roberts' approach is likely to be a significant&nbsp;
departure from the previous six films, which were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:53.280
all directed by Paul W.S. Anderson. No release&nbsp;
date has been announced for the Resident Evil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.280 --> 00:13:00.000
prequel, but filming began in October of 2020,&nbsp;
and it's expected to hit screens sometime in 2021.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:05.680
More than three decades after the original&nbsp;
Troop Beverly Hills hit theaters in 1989,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:10.720
a sequel is in the works from Israeli filmmaker&nbsp;
Oran Zegman, in her feature directorial debut.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.960
The original Troop Beverly Hills film starred&nbsp;
Shelley Long as a pampered housewife on the brink&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:19.440
of divorce, who sets out to prove to her family&nbsp;
that she's capable of more than they think by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:24.880
becoming a Wilderness Girls den mother. There's no&nbsp;
word yet on whether the original cast will return,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:30.560
or even what the sequel is about, but Ava Fries —&nbsp;
whose real-life experiences inspired the events of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:35.280
the first movie — is back on board as executive&nbsp;
producer, indicating that the sequel could also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:39.200
draw from some part of her life, although&nbsp;
nothing official has yet been announced.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:44.560
While the main Toy Story narrative appears to&nbsp;
have been wrapped up by the end of Toy Story 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:48.160
it seems that Pixar aren't ready to&nbsp;
say goodbye to the franchise just yet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:53.600
Disney announced during their 2020 Investor Day&nbsp;
event that everyone's favorite Space Ranger, Buzz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:59.440
Lightyear, would be getting his own feature film,&nbsp;
which will arrive in theaters June 17th, 2022.

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:02.880
But Lightyear won't be your typical&nbsp;
spinoff. Instead of following the Tim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.280
Allen-voiced character from the Toy Story films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:09.760
Lightyear will follow a different Buzz&nbsp;
Lightyear, voiced by MCU star Chris Evans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:14.960
After Pixar tweeted that the movie will be "the&nbsp;
definitive story of the original Buzz Lightyear,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:18.320
Evans followed their announcement up&nbsp;
with a clarification of his own, saying:

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:21.600
"And just to be clear, this&nbsp;
isn't Buzz Lightyear the toy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:26.240
This is the origin story of the human&nbsp;
Buzz Lightyear that the toy is based on."

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:31.280
Basically, this is the movie on which the&nbsp;
Buzz Lightyear toys are based. Expect plenty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:36.160
of sci-fi heroics, thrilling space action,&nbsp;
and, hopefully, an appearance from this guy.

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:39.280
"I'll never give in. You killed my father!"

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:43.840
"No, Buzz. I am your father."

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:45.040
"Noooooo!"

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:52.800
In a normal year, a movie like The War With&nbsp;
Grandpa probably wouldn't have delivered an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:58.480
especially notable performance at the box office.&nbsp;
But in 2020, when many theaters were operating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:03.520
at extremely limited capacity, the movie was a&nbsp;
surprising success — since it was basically one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:08.880
the only ones anybody could actually see. Still,&nbsp;
that's apparently enough to warrant a sequel.

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:12.960
Starring Robert De Niro alongside an&nbsp;
all-star cast, The War With Grandpa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:16.400
follows a kid who is upset about having&nbsp;
to give up his room to his grandfather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:20.880
and decides to wage war in order to reclaim it.&nbsp;
Although the film ends with the two in a better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:25.360
place, the sequel will apparently revisit the&nbsp;
family when Grandpa proposes to his girlfriend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:30.640
and needs to meet her family from London. While&nbsp;
there's no word yet on a release date just yet, we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:36.160
can only hope that, when it finally does release,&nbsp;
it will be under far less harrowing circumstances.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:42.240
Although a G.I. Goe spinoff titled Snake Eyes&nbsp;
was delayed until 2021 due to the coronavirus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:47.360
pandemic, that hasn't stopped Paramount from&nbsp;
moving forward with yet another G.I. Joe sequel.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:52.000
While no plot or casting details for the&nbsp;
third G.I. Joe film have been confirmed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:56.240
back in 2018 it was reported that the&nbsp;
title would be G.I. Joe: Ever Vigilant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:59.280
and that it would star Dwayne Johnson,&nbsp;
reprising his role from G.I. Joe:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:03.360
Retaliation. Of course, at the time that those&nbsp;
details were announced, Mission Impossible:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:08.160
Ghost Protocol writers Josh Appelbaum and Andre&nbsp;
Nemec were also attached to write the script,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:12.800
which is no longer the case. With the script&nbsp;
changing hands, it's very possible that none of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:17.440
the other previously announced details are still&nbsp;
the case — but we'll likely find out soon enough.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:22.080
Having announced that the absurdly&nbsp;
successful Transformers franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:27.280
will be stepping in a new direction, Paramount are&nbsp;
eyeing up Creed II director Steven Caple Jr. to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:32.080
helm the next movie in the franchise. Caple will&nbsp;
be working from a script written by Joby Harold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:35.680
who was responsible for the screenplay&nbsp;
for King Arthur: Legend of the Sword&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:39.680
and will be serving as a writer for the&nbsp;
upcoming Obi-Wan Kenobi series at Disney+.

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:45.840
While a deal hasn't closed quite yet, production&nbsp;
insiders told Deadline that Caple was the top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:50.560
choice among studio executives and producers.&nbsp;
Although Paramount hasn't yet revealed anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:55.440
definitive about the plot or characters for&nbsp;
Transformers 7, producer Lorenzo Di Bonaventura&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:59.360
previously revealed that the studio wasn't&nbsp;
interested in developing a direct sequel to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:04.640
The Last Knight — and that the next Transformers&nbsp;
film won't be picking up where that one left off.

